{"name":"Tourmaline","hex":"#83a1a7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tourmaline","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complex black or dark-coloured borosilicate mineral, compounded with various chemical elements and considered a semi-precious stone.","A transparent gemstone cut from it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tourmaline"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tourmaline","blocks":[{"text":"Tourmaline is a crystalline silicate mineral group in which boron is compounded with elements such as aluminium, iron, magnesium, sodium, lithium, or potassium. This gemstone comes in a wide variety of colors."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Tourmaline-121240.jpg/330px-Tourmaline-121240.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tourmaline"},{"title":"Tourmaline (activist)","blocks":[{"text":"Tourmaline is an American artist, filmmaker, activist, editor, and writer. She is a transgender woman who identifies as queer. Tourmaline is most notable for her work in transgender activism and economic justice, through her work with the Sylvia Rivera Law Project, Critical Resistance and Queers for Economic Justice. She is based in New York City."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Tourmaline_2025_Texas_Book_Festival.jpg/330px-Tourmaline_2025_Texas_Book_Festival.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tourmaline_(activist)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Tourmaline_gisements.jpg/500px-Tourmaline_gisements.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Tourmaline_gisements.jpg/1280px-Tourmaline_gisements.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikime